## CONVERSATION

<USER_REQUEST>
How do the mTOR inhibitors work?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
mTOR inhibitors are a class of drugs that target the mechanistic mTOR (mammalian target of protein kinase C) pathway. mTOR is a serine kinase that plays a crucial role in cell growth, proliferation, and differentiation. It is a key component of two signaling complexes: mTOR-1 and mTOR-2. mTOR inhibitors are used in the treatment of certain cancers and other diseases where mTOR signaling is overregulated. mTOR inhibitors are classified into two main classes: inhibitors of mTOR-1 and inhibitors that inhibit both mTOR-1 and mTOR-2. mTOR-1 is the primary target of these drugs.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

