","Chronic stress can significantly affect the functionality of natural killer cells (NK cells) in the immune system. NK cells are a type of immune cell that play a crucial role in the immune system by recognizing and killing cells that are damaged, damaged, or cancerous. They are essential for the elimination of pathogens and the maintenance of immune homeostasis.

