1. Corticoid production: Chronic stress can lead to the overproduction of neurotransmitters like dopamine and norepinephrine, which in turn stimulate the release of glucocorticoids (such as cortisol) from the adrenal glands. Glucocorticoids are known to have a negative impact on NK cell activity by:

