The effect of corticosteroids on the growth-promoting action of somrotropin is generally antagonistic, meaning they can reduce the effectiveness of somrotropin. Cortrogens are known to inhibit the growth of the adrenal gland, which can lead to a decrease in the production of sex hormones, such as estrogen and testosterone, which are essential for growth and development. Cortrogens can also inhibit the growth of other tissues, such as the heart, lungs, and bones.

