E_cell ≈ 0.34 - 0.00417 * (-2.3026)
E_cell ≈ 0.34 + 0.0097
E_cell ≈ 0.3497 V

Next, we need to find the current (I) of the cell. The current is related to the cell potential and the charge (Q) of the current flow over time (t) using the formula:

I = Q/t

Assuming a steady current, we can use the current (I) to calculate the power output (P):

P = I * E_cell

