   - The train takes 25 seconds to pass the joguer, so:
     \[
     \text{Distance} = \text{Relative Speed} \times \text{Time}
     \]
     \[
     150 + x = 10 \times 25
     \]
     \[
     150 + x = 250
     \]
     \[
     x = 250 - 150 = 100 \text{ m}
     \]

5. **Final Answer:**
   - The train is \(\boxed{100 \text{ m}}\) long.
