\[
\text{Total} = \text{Two-car guitar} + \text{In-ground swimming pool} - \text{Both} + \text{Neither}
\]
\[
\text{Total} = G + S - \text{Both} + N
\]
\[
90 = 50 + 40 - \text{Both} + 35
\]
\[
90 = 125 - \text{Both}
\]
\[
\text{Both} = 125 - 90 = 35
\]

Thus, the number of heads with both a two-car guitar and an in-ground swimming pool is $\boxed{35}$.
