     \[
     E_{\text{HMTD}} = \frac{3}{2} \times 1.0 \times 10^6 \text{ Pa} \times 1.0 \times 10^{-3} \text{ m}^3 = 1500 \text{ J}
     \]

2. **Account for the 70% energy in the pressure wave:**
   - Only 70% of the energy is in the pressure wave, so:
     \[
     E_{\text{pressure}} = 0.7 \times 1500 \text{ J} = 1050 \text{ J}
     \]

