   - Cylinder A: \( A_A = \frac{\pi}{4} \times (100 \, \text{mm})^2 = \frac{\pi}{4} \times (0.1 \, \, \text{m})^2 = 0.0314 \, \text{m}^2 \)
   - Cylinder B: \( A_B = \frac{\pi}{4} \times (25 \, \text{mm})^2 = \frac{\pi}{4} \times (0.025 \, \, \text{m})^2 = 0.000625 \, \text{m}^2 \)

2. **Calculate the weight of the piston:**
   - \( W = m \times g = 25 \, \text{kg} \times 9.807 \, \text{m/s}^2 = 245.175 \, \text{N} \)

3. **Equilibrium Condition:**
   The pressure in cylinder B \( P_B \) must balance the weight of the piston and the external atmospheric pressure \( P_{\text{atm}} \):
   \[
   P_B = \frac{W}{A_B} + P_{\text{atm}}
   \]
